#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549091} :activity/id #uuid "0e84b2fb-4cf2-5c9f-98bb-5999f15e2bd4" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048253 :topic/id #uuid "8c8ae3a5-d4bd-50b8-9f66-a4a042bb870c" :topic/math-academy-id 4143} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549086 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278545 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b71688e-a084-50b0-8ee6-cfbf6ebd32af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3e-{e}^{-1}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275872} {:answer/id #uuid "4431028f-ab75-5b42-a52f-32fd75e489e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-1}-e}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276079} {:answer/id #uuid "745d7976-0dbc-50a2-9490-bc45b40b9a87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{5e+2{e}^{-1}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276530} {:answer/id #uuid "89b5e633-6fda-572c-a63c-6a89752bac4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7e-{e}^{-1}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276721} {:answer/id #uuid "b0b62c25-f5f9-5ac7-a005-6cbd37efb361" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{3e+{e}^{-1}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277057}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276079} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b538e17-dfb5-54b8-b49d-76ddb3c1edcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277774}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d858f67e-e87d-5922-848f-1cf10db83bc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-161536" :question/problem "Calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,0⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z={e}^{x}$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x})={e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x})=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the flux of $F$ through $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,0⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,0⟩{|}_{z={e}^{x}} \\\\  & =⟨{{y}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{x+{e}^{x}}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{0}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,0⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-y\\cdot ({e}^{x})-(x+{e}^{x})\\cdot 0+0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-y{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-y{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[-\\frac{{y}^{2}{e}^{x}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{[{e}^{x}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-1}-e}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "21e5af0d-5744-5b51-88fc-a24cd228d975"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549091 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423121 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65b0d9ca-824a-5dcc-9c38-6fd9b637f302" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-4P$ and $-2Q$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423096} {:answer/id #uuid "92e3c6dc-2a2e-5a89-badd-5c261850de58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-2P$ and $-Q$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423102} {:answer/id #uuid "c4841ceb-b2a6-58c8-96a9-bc8ce5fca6d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-4Q$ and $P$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423106} {:answer/id #uuid "f0f8eac7-f04f-5d8d-a984-6504f0ab8abc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-2R$ and $Q$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423112} {:answer/id #uuid "f233c1ca-3c84-5c07-9f36-b49ccdff39a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$P$ and $-R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423113}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423102} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4de48c6-077d-5787-a098-9c9aedaea635" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423117}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "431ed508-ca53-50c3-b7a4-875fc9b23084" :question/math-academy-id "q-161449" :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $z={x}^{2}y$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\,xy+\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\,{x}^{2}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $z={x}^{2}y,$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=⟨x,\\,y,\\,{x}^{2}y⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2xy⟩ \\\\ {r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,{x}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2xy \\\\ 0 & 1 & {x}^{2}\\end{aligned}|=⟨-2xy,\\,-{x}^{2},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,y))\\cdot ({r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨-2xy,\\,-{x}^{2},\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-2P\\,xy+(\\,-Q\\,)\\,{x}^{2}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "4105b6fe-4490-51ed-ab36-ff7ad9a443aa" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549142}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549142 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278519 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11e71243-92a0-5d43-b5a3-d37e9d9577d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-Q,\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂z},\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275638} {:answer/id #uuid "1733f81c-8c75-5995-ad54-2ab255bb13b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-Q,\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂x},\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275694} {:answer/id #uuid "2cfc931d-121f-57c0-ac5c-fdc2916d3343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-Q,\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275883} {:answer/id #uuid "3a8033d3-73a6-5faf-9ba8-27ae7a3acd02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "Q,\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275991} {:answer/id #uuid "4f2411ed-300b-54b9-9625-f35ce1fd17dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "Q,\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276182}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276182} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fceae9a-bc1a-5dd0-a3ba-10a17494da0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "46dbd1e0-5399-5e33-b950-1f08b8d717ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-161465" :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $x=k(y,z)$ for $(y,z)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(P-\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\,\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}-R\\,\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $x=k(y,z),$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(y,z)=⟨k(y,z),\\,y,\\,z⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{z}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂k}{∂z},\\,0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{y}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂k}{∂y} & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{∂k}{∂z} & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|=⟨1,\\,-\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\,-\\frac{∂k}{∂z}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,y))\\cdot ({r}_{y}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,-\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\,-\\frac{∂k}{∂z}⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(P-Q\\,\\frac{∂k}{∂y}-R\\,\\frac{∂k}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "c55337c0-db12-5a83-8b19-0b1d1ecef642" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549086}}] :activity/title "Calculating Flux Through Cartesian Surfaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548337}]}
